NNAAMMEE
       pamtable - print the raster as a table of numerical sample values


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaammttaabbllee

       [_n_e_t_p_b_m_f_i_l_e]



DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammttaabbllee  prints  the  raster of a Netpbm image as a table of numerical
       sample values.  For example,  a  5-pixel  wide,  2-pixel  high  rainbow
       (black, red, green, blue, white) PPM image with maxval 255 would appear
       as follows:



               0   0   0|255   0   0|  0 255   0|  0   0 255|255 255 255
               0   0   0|255   0   0|  0 255   0|  0   0 255|255 255 255




       If you care to see only certain rows or columns, use ppaammccuutt  to  filter
       the input.

       If  you  care  to see only certain planes, use ppaammcchhaannnneell to filter the
       input.

       ppaammttaabbllee prints vertical bars between tuples, unless there is only  one
       sample  per  tuple,  in which case it prints a single space between tu‐
       ples.

       ppaammttaabbllee prints a single space between samples within a tuple.

       For each sample, ppaammttaabbllee prints the numerical value  from  the  Netpbm
       image,  uninterpreted.  It prints it in decimal, right justified in the
       minimum number of spaces required to print the maxval of the image.

       If you want the samples to print more densely, use ppaammddeepptthh  to  reduce
       the maxval (thus making the decimal numbers for the samples narrower).

       The  lleessss program (not part of Netpbm) is good for browsing through the
       table.  Use its ----cchhoopp--lloonngg--lliinneess option and use cursor  movement  keys
       to scroll around in the image.



AARRGGUUMMEENNTTSS
       The only possible argument is the name of the file containing the input
       Netpbm image.  This is optional; if you don't  specify  any  arguments,
       the input comes from Standard Input.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There  are  no  command line options defined specifically for ppaammttaabbllee,
       but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)


